(EXP-29: a cast binds tighter than arithmetic and applies to the expression
 immediately to its left.
 Also covers: EXP-30, bracing to cast a whole arithmetic expression.
 The two floats are chosen so the two readings differ: tight binding gives
 3.5 add {2.5 as a number} = 5.5, loose binding would give 6. The third line
 is the manual's own `n as a number add 1` shape on a text, which only
 compiles at all under tight binding, since text arithmetic is EXP-11.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-29.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   5.5
   6
   11
)
a float called half is 2.5.
a float called seedling is 3.5.
a text called tally is "10".
Print seedling add half as a number.
Print {seedling add half} as a number.
Print tally as a number add 1.
